+/*
+ * One whole frame at a time. The rawvideo reader in the encoder takes a short
+ * read as a corrupt packet ("Invalid buffer size ... < expected frame_size")
+ * and throws the whole input away, so a frame is never left half written: the
+ * write waits for the encoder to drain, and only gives up when the encoder is
+ * gone or the budget is spent.
